## Caching

Compiled with `--with-caching`. The cache is located by `WT_CACHE__STORE`; with it
unset every step simply runs. Only the sequential DAG caches — an async method
hands back a future, which has no stored form — so the async DAG is generated
without caching. Each run writes `cache-report.json` beside
`result.json` — even when the run fails — saying what each step's cache did
and why, and where a failed run stopped.

A step's code identity is the task distribution's installed version plus a
fingerprint of its dependency closure. An editable install — a local checkout
wired in through `wt-compiler-env-overrides.toml`, say — freezes that version
string at install time, so editing task code afterwards moves no key, and a
warm run keeps serving what the old code produced. That is intended rather
than a bug: changing a task's signature or the shape of its return type still
invalidates, but changing its body does not. While developing against a
checkout, set `WT_CACHE__EPOCH` to something that moves with the code — the
checkout's git sha, or a number you bump by hand — or clear the `WT_CACHE__STORE`
store.

Full documentation: https://github.com/wildlife-dynamics/wt/blob/main/docs/content/caching.md
